WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.080
My favorite activity!

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.620
3, 2 ,1

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:09.760
(Peter the intern dies a lot.)

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.860
Blackmagic, they make DaVinci Resolve, and DaVinci is a free colorgrading program

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.360
It works really well. One of the guys there saw our Star Wars drone video,

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.760
"You guys need some sick cameras for putting on drones"

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:27.960
They have sent us a Blackmagic Micro Cinema Camera, basically a little action camera.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.120
So, think like of a GoPro but a lot more cinematic.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.040
[Plastic ripped to shreds. To shreds, you say?]

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.640
Ooh, look at how tiny this guy is.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.560
Wow, that's really cool, actually.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.080
Dude, this is like maximum efficiency of technology right here.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.260
Sweet, I can't wait to fire this up. Let's get some T E S T   I M A G E S !

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.160
A few months ago, I was opening up the door to our studio, and Wren was on the other side,

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.700
And he fired a Nerf gun at me, and as that dart came flying towards my face, I thought,

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.160
"I could do this. I could be a total badass."

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:56.400
And I reached up and I snatched that Nerf dart out of the air before it hit me in the eye.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.660
I'm wondering, is that something really easy to do, or is it actually almost impossible?

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.420
Do we all have secret ninja skills?

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:05.060
We're going to up on the roof, and we're all going to shoot Nerf guns at each other's faces,

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.860
and see if we have the ability to snatch Nerf darts out of the air.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:09.400
Let's go.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.240
[Cool transition, bro]

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.480
Alright. Try to shoot me in the face!

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:13.380
[Hearty chuckles]

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.600
My pleasure!

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.800
[A very weak shot]

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.760
THIS GUN SUCKS!

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.020
[gun gets smashed on ground]

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.080
3, 2, 1!

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:37.360
None of the darts even hit me, so I wouldn't have even had to catch them.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:40.020
I was just being efficient with my use of energy.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.300
A pro would have caught them.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.780
3, 2, 1!

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.480
The fuck is that?!

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.520
3, 2, 1!

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.900
What the hell, dude?

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.400
3, 2, 1!

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.920
OOOOOAAAAAAAHHHHHHHAOHOHOHAOHOHWHOHOHOHOWWOHAOHHAHOWHOAHOWHAAOOOOH

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:56.780
What was that?!

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.580
Ooooohhwoooooaahhhhwoooaaaaahhh!

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:00.720
[bite off head of dart, chewed up, and spit out]

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.140
I didn't even have to move my hand; I just had to close it.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:04.760
No.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:06.660
No.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.820
Pvwwwhhhhzuuuuu, schwing!

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:25.360
3, 2, 1!

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.440
Oh, you went right for my face!

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.480
Hehe, I did that on purpose.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:31.560
Arrows? Ain't no thang.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.660
3, 2, 1!

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.120
Wooaaah!

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.080
3, 2, 1!

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.400
Twice in a row!

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.280
One!

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.540
I'm going for four for four!

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.100
That one was a fastball. Schwooo!

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.400
They call three-four, for short. Thirty four.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:05.240
I have been tasked with putting together this Blackmagic Micro Cinema Camera.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.060
I'm putting it together, because Niko asked me to.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.220
I think I just needed to have a job sent to me.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:10.940
Oh, there's the light.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.720
Woah, you can see the sensor.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.700
We need to get a monitor for this.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:16.660
Okay.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:19.780
There it goes.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.260
I say we put a lens on the camera.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.460
This is an adapter.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:23.680
It will line up the red dots.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:25.300
There we go.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.020
This is hilarious.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.680
This is called an Israeli arm.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:32.340
You always do things the most efficient way.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.900
I'm gonna grab an arrow like this as it flies by.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.500
3, 2, 1!

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:58.700
YEEEAAAAHH-woo-AAAAAAHHHH-woo!

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.980
So, Wren here is back from Vietnam finally.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:05.240
Wow, so everyone's caught an arrow. Yep.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.340
I have to not fail here.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:11.000
Just walking along, minding my own business, but suddenly Wren pops out. Wren!

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.400
Wren's dead.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.400
Alright. Ok, I'm going to shoot you, Niko.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.540
Alright, let's do this!

